# additions.allow - every POST line with no PRE origin, declared and typed (C5, F3/F8).
#
# Types:
#   pointer   a D2 call-site pointer. Asserted MECHANICALLY against the form
#             `**<Trigger>** - read `<FILE>.md` (*<Original section heading>*)`,
#             not merely listed.
#   stanza    a split's new carved-body heading, or the intake skeleton's heading.
#   ~ changed a REWORDED line, written as a PAIRED block:
#                 ~ changed
#                 - <the PRE line, verbatim>
#                 + <the POST line that replaces it>
#             Subtracted from BOTH channels: from C1 (so a replaced line is not
#             "lost") and from C5 (so its replacement is not "fabricated"). A `-`
#             without its `+`, or a `+` without its `-`, FAILS - an unpaired half
#             is exactly how a deletion masquerades as a move.
#
# Format for pointer/stanza: <type> TAB <the exact line>
#
# NO PHASE IN THIS CAMPAIGN EXERCISES A `changed` PAIR (D7). The three `](#...)`
# links were rewritten in the standalone pre-carve commit fdfad28 and the baseline
# was re-pinned behind it, so every carve step is a verbatim move of lines already
# in final form. The pairing mechanism stays in the model and in the self-test
# (mutation 4 proves it fires), but a non-zero `~ changed` count here is a STOP
# that returns to the user - it means a substitution landed inside a mapped range,
# which is the interaction this campaign deliberately has no machinery for.
#
# Archived to tests/carve/additions.<slug>.allow at merge, and the baseline
# re-pins to the merge commit (D5).
#
# Empty at Phase 1b: nothing has been carved, so nothing has been added.
